pageId: connect2wow
title: "Connect2WOW · Case Study"
description: "How an ERP decides what deserves your attention. A design system for an enterprise ERP, told through its notification subsystem."
project: connect2wow
permalink: /work/connect2wow/
---
{#
  CONNECT2WOW — Figma 296:11457. Six bands on the shared new-design shell; see
  src/work/onton.njk for the band model.

  WHAT IS NEW HERE:
    · a five-column research table with multi-line cells and a logo per row —
      denser than either previous table
    · three numbered design principles, each pairing a claim with a live
      visualization, split by rules
    · an Outcome band of two spec sheets, the second of them pre-clipped

  WHAT IS ABSENT, and deliberately: no stats row, no delta chips, no persona
  system. The page ends on one long paragraph because the project shut down
  before launch and there are no numbers to end on.
#}

{% from "components/media-slot.njk" import mediaSlot, markSlot, embedSlot %}

{# ---- 1. COVER — 296:11471 ----------------------------------------------- #}
<section class="case-band case-band--cover" aria-labelledby="c2w-title">
  <div class="case-band__inner">
    {#- BREADCRUMB — 550:11647. One 100-tall row carrying what used to be two:
        the back link and the eyebrow lockup. <nav> because it is navigation to
        somewhere else on the site, and the aria-label is what distinguishes it
        from the site nav in a landmark list.

        THE SEPARATOR RIDES INSIDE THE CRUMB IT FOLLOWS. Two links, two slashes,
        none trailing — the count is structural rather than something a loop
        index has to get right. Each is aria-hidden: it is punctuation between
        list items, and the list already says "3 items" out loud. -#}
    <nav class="case-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a
        class="case-crumbs__back"
        href="{{ connect2wow.cover.backHref }}"
        aria-label="{{ connect2wow.cover.backLabel }}"
      >{{ markSlot(connect2wow.cover.chevron) }}</a>

      <ol class="case-crumbs__list" role="list">
        {%- for c in connect2wow.cover.crumbs %}
          <li class="case-crumbs__item">
            <a class="case-crumbs__link" href="{{ c.href }}">{{ c.label }}</a>
            <span class="case-crumbs__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
          </li>
        {%- endfor %}
        <li class="case-crumbs__item">
          {{ markSlot(connect2wow.cover.mark) }}
          <span class="case-crumbs__current" aria-current="page">{{ connect2wow.cover.eyebrow }}</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    {{ mediaSlot(connect2wow.cover.media) }}

    <div class="case-cover__row">
      <h1 class="case-cover__headline" id="c2w-title">{{ connect2wow.cover.headline }}</h1>
      <p class="case-cover__intro">
        {%- for part in connect2wow.cover.intro -%}
          <span class="case-tone--{{ part.tone }}">{{ part.text }}</span>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---- 2. CHALLENGE / OBJECTIVE / ROLE / OUTCOME — 296:11482 -------------- #}
<section class="case-band case-band--facets" aria-label="Project summary">
  <div class="case-band__inner case-band__inner--flush">
    <div class="case-facets">
      {%- for f in connect2wow.facets %}
        <div class="case-facet">
          <h3 class="case-facet__label">{{ f.label }}</h3>
          <p class="case-facet__body">
            {#- Same shape as the cover intro just above: one plain string, or an
                array of {text, tone} runs. All four of these are inked in part
                (296:11489 / 11493 / 11498 / 11502). -#}
            {%- if f.body is string -%}
              {{ f.body }}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- for part in f.body -%}
                <span class="case-tone--{{ part.tone }}">{{ part.text }}</span>
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          </p>
        </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---- 3. RESEARCH INSIGHTS — 296:11503 ----------------------------------- #}
<section class="case-band" aria-labelledby="c2w-research">
  <div class="case-band__inner">
    {#- A full-width paragraph before the heading, unique to this band. -#}
    <p class="case-note">{{ connect2wow.research.lead }}</p>

    <div class="case-headrow">
      <h2 class="case-heading" id="c2w-research">{{ connect2wow.research.heading }}</h2>
      <p class="case-deck">{{ connect2wow.research.deck }}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="case-panel">
      <table class="case-table case-table--research">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            {%- for col in connect2wow.research.columns %}
              <th scope="col">
                {#- The comp's first header holds an invisible spacer; nothing
                    is rendered there but the column still needs a name. -#}
                {%- if col %}{{ col }}{% else %}<span class="case-table__hidden">Design system</span>{% endif -%}
              </th>
            {%- endfor %}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {%- for row in connect2wow.research.rows %}
            <tr>
              <th scope="row" class="case-table__product">
                {{ markSlot(row.mark) }}
                <span>{{ row.name }}</span>
              </th>
              {%- for cell in row.cells %}
                <td>{{ cell }}</td>
              {%- endfor %}
            </tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="case-note">{{ connect2wow.research.anchor }}</p>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---- 4. DESIGN PRINCIPLES — 296:11568 ----------------------------------- #}
{#
  Flush: the heading block and each principle carry their own padding, and the
  rules between them are the band's own structure rather than gaps.
#}
<section class="case-band case-band--principles" aria-labelledby="c2w-principles">
  <div class="case-band__inner case-band__inner--flush">
    <div class="c2w-principles__head">
      <h2 class="case-heading" id="c2w-principles">{{ connect2wow.principles.heading }}</h2>
    </div>

    {#- An ordered list, because the numerals are the comp's list markers and
        the three principles are a sequence, not three unrelated claims. -#}
    <ol class="c2w-principles">
      {%- for p in connect2wow.principles.items %}
        <li class="c2w-principle">
          <div class="c2w-principle__text">
            <p class="c2w-principle__body">
              <strong>{{ p.lead }}</strong><br />{{ p.rest }}
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="c2w-principle__media" style="--principle-pad: {{ p.pad }}">
            {{ embedSlot(p.embed) }}
          </div>
        </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---- 5. OUTCOME — 296:11776 --------------------------------------------- #}
<section class="case-band case-band--outcome" aria-labelledby="c2w-outcome">
  <div class="case-band__inner case-band__inner--flush">
    <div class="c2w-outcome__head">
      <h2 class="case-heading" id="c2w-outcome">{{ connect2wow.outcome.heading }}</h2>
      <p class="case-deck">{{ connect2wow.outcome.body }}</p>
    </div>

    {#-
      A FIXED-HEIGHT BANNER. 60 of padding plus a 467-tall group is this band's
      527 exactly, so nothing spills — the cut in the second sheet is baked into
      its export, not made here. Keep the height fixed regardless.
    -#}
    <div class="c2w-panels" style="--panels-h: {{ connect2wow.outcome.panelsHeight }}">
      <div class="c2w-panels__group">
        {%- for panel in connect2wow.outcome.panels %}
          <div class="c2w-panel">
            {%- if panel.heading %}
              <div class="c2w-panel__head">
                <h3 class="c2w-panel__heading">{{ panel.heading }}</h3>
                <p class="c2w-panel__subtitle">{{ panel.subtitle }}</p>
              </div>
            {%- endif %}
            {{ mediaSlot(panel.media) }}
          </div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---- 6. REFLECTION — 296:12041 ------------------------------------------ #}
<section class="case-band" aria-labelledby="c2w-reflection">
  <div class="case-band__inner">
    <div class="case-headrow case-headrow--stacked">
      <h2 class="case-heading" id="c2w-reflection">{{ connect2wow.reflection.heading }}</h2>
      {#- One line of space between paragraphs, as the comp's blank lines set
          it — margin rather than empty elements. -#}
      <div class="c2w-reflection">
        {%- for para in connect2wow.reflection.body %}
          <p class="case-deck">{{ para }}</p>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
